<Layout
	title="Digital Sovereignty"
	description="Reclaiming your digital infrastructure from the cloud giants. Cloud Exit Audits, Sovereignty Analytics, and homestead FOSS stacks on hardware you own."
	pubDate={new Date()}
	heroImage="/og-default.png"
>
	<h1>Digital Sovereignty</h1>
	<p>
		The modern business is held hostage by the cloud. Renting your own operations back from corporations that can raise prices, change terms, or shut the door whenever it suits them. We help you take it back.
	</p>

	<h2 class="service">Sovereignty Analytics <span class="flag">The Headliner</span></h2>
	<p>
		Enterprise KPI culture without the enterprise software bill. FOSS dashboards (Metabase, Grafana) replacing your Power BI/Tableau subscriptions, wired to automated SQL/Python reporting pipelines. Daily visibility, weekly scorecards, monthly reviews — on hardware you own, with zero license fees.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>The receipts, because we sell with receipts, not promises:</strong> 1,300+ FTE hours/year saved through a single claim-system automation. 10+ regional reports automated in Python. The first ocean-container visibility report rolled out globally. A mobile-printing SOP that scaled across every North American distribution center. Fifteen years of supply chain and analytics work, pointed at your business.
	</p>

	<h2 class="service">Cloud Exit Audits</h2>
	<p>
		A flat-fee analysis of your current cloud spend to identify waste, vendor lock-in, and dependency risk — then a concrete migration roadmap back to hardware you actually own. Every audit comes with the <a href="/catalog">FOSS Sovereignty Catalog</a>: a curated menu of open-source replacements for the SaaS you're bleeding on.
	</p>
	<p>
		No bespoke one-offs, no open-ended engagements. Audits run as capped quarterly sprints — two a month, max. Past the ceiling, there's a waitlist, not overtime.
	</p>

	<h2 class="service">Homestead Implementation</h2>
	<p>
		Self-hosted FOSS stacks built on refurbished, enterprise-grade hardware — the power of the cloud with the sovereignty of a home lab. Salvage iron on a renewable tariff: the greenest computer is the one that already exists.
	</p>

	<h2 class="service">Device Reclamation</h2>
	<p>
		'Obsolete' electronics reborn as sovereign tools: gaming and music cyberdecks, dedicated home-lab controllers, secure locked-down devices for your kids. <strong>Guided builds on your own hardware</strong> — we teach the process, you own the result and the skills to repeat it.
	</p>

	<h2 class="service">The Guardian Retainer (Sovereign Continuity)</h2>
	<p>
		Peace of mind for the sovereign. For SMBs, we pivot from simple maintenance to <strong>Sovereign Continuity</strong>: removing "Key Person Risk" and ensuring business continuity through living documentation. Hard cap of 3–5 clients, premium pricing, application-only — backed by a career of managing $1M+ assets and high-stakes operational risk. Scheduled maintenance windows, defined in writing. Not on-call heroics. Past the cap: waitlist, not overtime.
	</p>

	<p>
		<em>Teach, Don't Vend:</em> no inventory, no hardware sales, no warranties on gear. Your device, your hands, our expertise. Reclaimed hardware exists as demo and proof — never product.
	</p>
</Layout>